   {
    "attribute": "arrangement",
    "likely_right_file": "bhel/Part1.pdf",
    "likely_right_page": 43,
    "why": "Both 2W+1S and 3X50% mean the same standard setup of two working 50% pumps and one standby pump, though Part 1 p.43 and Part 4 p.59 give the fuller equipment specification.",
    "consequence": "Because the original system is only sized for two working pumps (100% total flow), running all three pumps together at 150% flow can overload the common piping, power supply, and downstream equipment, and leaves no backup pump if one fails."
